{
  "answer": "If the Payments Database goes down, the following services will be affected:\n\n1. **Payment Service**: This service is critical for handling all financial transactions and directly depends on the Payments Database for transaction storage (relationship: Payment Service --[DEPENDS_ON]--> Payments Database).\n\n2. **Fraud Detection Service**: This service performs real-time fraud detection for payment transactions and queries historical transactions from the Payments Database (relationship: Fraud Detection Service --[DEPENDS_ON]--> Payments Database).\n\n3. **Checkout Service**: Although it primarily depends on the Order Database, the Checkout Service orchestrates payment processing, which relies on the Payment Service. Therefore, if the Payments Database is down, it will indirectly affect the Checkout Service's ability to complete transactions (relationship: Checkout Service --[DEPENDS_ON]--> Payment Service).\n\nIn summary, the Payment Service and Fraud Detection Service will be directly impacted, while the Checkout Service will be indirectly affected due to its reliance on the Payment Service.",
